The code statements that lead to the bug are:
validated_shader->uniform_addr_offsets = krealloc(...);
Reason:
Directly overwriting the original pointer with the return value of krealloc() loses the previous allocation if krealloc() fails (returns NULL), causing a memory leak.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
offsets = krealloc_array(validated_shader->uniform_addr_offsets, o + 1, sizeof(...), GFP_KERNEL);
if (!offsets) return false;
validated_shader->uniform_addr_offsets = offsets;
Reason:
A temporary variable holds the return value of krealloc() (or krealloc_array()) so the original pointer is preserved if allocation fails. The original pointer is updated only after a successful allocation, preventing the memory leak.

